# HSM collector conformance v1 — metric-source failures and the disk-space prediction (#1426).
# Format: case|action|arg1|arg2|...
# Wall-clock fixture.
#
# Actions introduced here:
# create_failing_metric_sensor|path|post_period_ms|message
#   A Double value sensor whose live read FAILS every tick with `message`, leaving the source
#   usable. Native binds a metric source that answers HSM_METRIC_READ_SAMPLE_ERROR; C# registers a
#   MonitoringSensorBase<double> whose GetValue throws the same message — the same seam, since
#   BuildSensorValue routes a throwing read to the error channel.
# create_disk_prediction_sensor|path|calibration_requests|post_period_ms|refresh_period_ms|free_space_start|drain_per_second
#   The "Free space on disk prediction" sensor over a SCRIPTED free-space series (free space changes
#   linearly with elapsed time), with fixture-sized periods; the catalog row runs 5 min posts,
#   10 min sampling and 3 calibration requests. C# registers FreeDiskSpacePredictionBase over a scripted
#   IDiskInfo; native binds a metric source running the same disk_prediction.hpp math.
#   `drain_per_second` is SIGNED: positive drains the disk, zero holds it flat, negative frees space
#   (#1445), which is how the idle and growing states below are reached.
#
# Contract notes:
# - A FAILED read is never silent (root rule #8). It lands in the collector's error channel — the
#   deduplicated error log and, when the host registered it, the `.module/Collector errors` sensor —
#   as "Sensor: <path>, <reason>". An EMPTY tick (a delta source seeding its baseline) is NOT a
#   failure and stays silent in both collectors.
# - A VALUE sensor whose read failed also posts one value per post period: the default value, status
#   Error (3), and the failure message as the comment. A BAR sensor posts nothing — it just skips
#   the sample. That split is managed's: BuildSensorValue's catch arm publishes the default value,
#   while CollectableBarMonitoringSensorBase simply takes no sample.
# - The prediction sensor runs two independent cadences: free space is sampled on its own period to
#   feed the SIGNED drain-speed EMA, and a TimeSpan is posted on the sensor's post period. In
#   production the sampling period is 10 min and the smoothing factor is 1/37, which puts the mean
#   age of the samples behind the estimate at exactly 6 h (#1445). Fixtures shrink both periods; the
#   factor is not a fixture knob, so a fixture asserts STATES and not smoothed numbers.
# - Exactly one of five states is posted (#1445), and only the first carries a real estimate:
#     draining below the ceiling  -> free_space / speed, Ok, "Free space decreases by X Mbytes/hour."
#     draining beyond the ceiling -> 365.00:00:00, OffTime, "... More than 365 days left."
#     not decreasing              -> 365.00:00:00, OffTime, "Free space is not decreasing. Value cannot be calculated."
#     increasing                  -> 365.00:00:00, OffTime, "Free space increases by X Mbytes/hour. Value cannot be calculated."
#     calibrating                 -> 365.00:00:00, OffTime, "Calibration request (n/N). Value cannot be calculated yet."
#   The ceiling stands for "no actionable estimate"; 00:00:00 is reserved for a disk with no free
#   space left and is never a placeholder, because an alert reads it as "full NOW".
# - X is the rate in MB/HOUR with up to six decimals, trailing zeros trimmed to at least one
#   (#1460), rounded from the same double by integer arithmetic in both collectors so the text
#   is byte-identical; it used to be MB/sec in shortest-round-trip form, which rendered a slow
#   drain as a 17-digit scientific literal. Six decimals because the "Mbytes" label is only
#   accurate on Windows (the Unix reader reports kB, so a Unix number is 1024x smaller than its
#   label), and three would round an ordinary Unix drain back to 0.000.
# - Calibration counts SAMPLES, not posts: (n/N) means n completed free-space measurements.
# - The NUMBER of calibration posts is deliberately NOT pinned. Managed starts its send loop in
#   InitAsync (first post due immediately) while the sampler's first tick is aligned to the next
#   period boundary, so how many posts precede the N-th sample depends on scheduling. That is a
#   lifecycle wrinkle, not a contract, and pinning it would pin a race.

# A read failure reaches `.module/Collector errors` and posts an Error-status value. The payload
# stream also carries the module group's own start markers, so both assertions are index-free.
metric_source_error_is_reported|create_collector
metric_source_error_is_reported|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
metric_source_error_is_reported|create_failing_metric_sensor|contract/metric/failing|300|proc read failed
metric_source_error_is_reported|start
metric_source_error_is_reported|expect_eventually_payload_contains|Collector errors","Value":"Sensor: |5
metric_source_error_is_reported|expect_eventually_payload_contains|proc read failed|5
metric_source_error_is_reported|expect_eventually_payload_contains|"Value":0,"Status":3,"Comment":"proc read failed"|5
metric_source_error_is_reported|stop

# 2 calibration requests, a post every 500 ms and a sample every 250 ms over 5.6 s: twelve posts
# nominally, which outruns the longest calibration opening either collector can produce (managed's
# is one longer than native's — see above), so the LAST payload is a settled prediction. Free space
# starts at 1 000 000 units and drains 1 000 per second, a strictly positive speed, so that
# prediction is a real (non-zero) TimeSpan rather than a repeat of the previous one.
# The lower count bound is load-bearing, not cosmetic: below 6 posts the tail can still be a
# calibration post, which carries the ceiling and would fail the last-payload assertion. The margin
# therefore lives in the sleep (12 nominal vs a floor of 6 tolerates half the posts slipping on a
# loaded runner), not in a looser bound.
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|create_collector
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction|2|500|250|1000000|1000
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|start
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|sleep_ms|5600
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|stop
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_sent_count_between|6|14|10
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|0|"Type":7
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|0|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|0|"Status":0
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|0|"Comment":"Calibration request (
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Type":7
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Status":1
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space decreases by
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_not_contains|-1|"Value":"00:00:00"
disk_prediction_calibrates_then_predicts|expect_payload_not_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"

# A disk that is NOT being written to (drain_per_second = 0) must say so, rather than repeat the
# last estimate or post zero (#1445). Every sample folds an exact 0 into the EMA, so the speed is
# exactly zero and the sensor settles in the "not decreasing" state.
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|create_collector
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction_idle|2|500|250|1000000|0
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|start
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|sleep_ms|5600
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|stop
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|expect_sent_count_between|6|14|10
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Type":7
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Status":0
disk_prediction_reports_no_drain_when_idle|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space is not decreasing. Value cannot be calculated."

# A disk that is being FREED (negative drain) reports growth. Before #1445 this branch was dead in
# both collectors, because a negative sample was discarded instead of folded into the EMA. The
# rendered rate depends on the wall-clock sampling intervals, so only the sentence is asserted.
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|create_collector
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction_growth|2|500|250|1000000|-1000
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|start
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|sleep_ms|5600
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|stop
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|expect_sent_count_between|6|14|10
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Type":7
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Status":0
disk_prediction_reports_growth_when_space_is_freed|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space increases by

# Calibration is counted on the SAMPLING clock (#1445). Posts every 200 ms against a 5 s sampling
# period: after 1.5 s there have been ~7 posts and AT MOST one measurement, so a 6-measurement
# calibration cannot possibly be over and the tail is still a calibration post carrying the ceiling.
# Counting posts instead - what the sensor used to do - would have finished calibration after 6
# posts (1.2 s) and started publishing an "estimate" built on one measurement or none.
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|create_collector
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction_calibration|6|200|5000|1000000|1000
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|start
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|sleep_ms|1500
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|stop
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Type":7
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Status":0
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Calibration request (
disk_prediction_calibration_counts_samples_not_posts|expect_payload_not_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space

# The 365-day ceiling (#1445), the fix for the overflow defect whose old symptom was the worst of
# the five: freeSpace / speed exceeded TimeSpan.MaxValue, FromSeconds threw, and the sensor posted
# NOTHING while still looking healthy. An exabyte draining at 1 MB/s is ~1e12 seconds, four orders
# of magnitude past the ceiling, so no scheduling jitter can move the state. The drain is kept large
# enough that a 250 ms interval is still a non-zero delta after the managed driver truncates free
# space to a long - a zero delta would land the case in the "not decreasing" state instead.
# The comment is OPERATOR-FACING text, so the rate has to be readable (#1460). It used to render
# MB/sec through the payload's shortest-round-trip formatter, which printed a realistic idle drain
# as "1.6574101944286661E-06 Mbytes/sec" - 17 digits of scientific notation in a sentence a human
# reads. It is now MB/HOUR with up to six decimals, rounded with integer arithmetic so both
# collectors emit the same bytes. This case drives a drain of 100 units/sec, which is ~0.34 MB/hour:
# small enough that the old format was scientific, large enough that a 250 ms interval survives the
# managed driver's truncation of free space to a long. The free space is far past the ceiling, so
# the state cannot drift. The DIGITS are not pinned (the EMA is wall-clock smoothed) - the SHAPE is:
# a decimal number, no exponent, MB/hour.
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|create_collector
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction_slow_drain|2|500|250|1000000000000|100
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|start
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|sleep_ms|2600
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|stop
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space decreases by 0.
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|expect_payload_contains|-1|Mbytes/hour. More than 365 days left.
disk_prediction_comment_reads_a_slow_drain_in_mb_per_hour|expect_payload_not_contains|-1|E-

disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|create_collector
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|create_disk_prediction_sensor|contract/metric/prediction_ceiling|2|500|250|1000000000000000000|1000000
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|start
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|sleep_ms|5600
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|stop
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_sent_count_between|6|14|10
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Type":7
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Value":"365.00:00:00"
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Status":0
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_payload_contains|-1|"Comment":"Free space decreases by
disk_prediction_clamps_a_trickle_drain_to_the_ceiling|expect_payload_contains|-1|More than 365 days left.
